win32u: the Unix side in the wasm64 module (docs/design/wine-unix.md,
sections 2, 3 and 7).

- syscall.c, stub_syscall (L39-61): the exception address is the guest
  CONTEXT's Rip, so its __x86_64__ branch gets || defined(__wasm64__)
  (section 3). Tempwind's table-1 stub wrappers stop loudly before it is
  reached (section 11), so this only keeps the code describing the guest.
- syscall.c: tw_win32u_unix_call_count, the entry count of
  __wine_unix_call_funcs (L108-111), as patch 0301 gives ntdll's
  tw_unix_call_count. The unix-call dispatcher checks a code against it
  through tw_unixlib_count (native/wine/src/unixlibs.c; section 11).
- winstation.c, map_shared_session_block (L106-144): block->data is
  tw_session_view(off, &size) (patch 0203) instead of a read-only view of
  \KernelObjects\__wine_session. off is Wine's offset rounded down to the
  allocation granularity (L114), and the size runs to the reservation's
  end, as Wine's view of size 0 runs to the section's end (L129-130), so
  find_shared_session_block's strict < (L157) keeps finding later objects
  in the same block. Its only caller is find_shared_session_block (L165),
  under session_lock, whose callers are find_shared_session_object (L182),
  for each shared object win32u reads, and shared_session_init (L197),
  which init_user calls (class.c L253), run once from
  NtUserInitializeClientPfnArrays (L263-279), user32's attach. On both paths the block is found or made as Wine's would be; a
  view before the server set the session up, or past the cap, stops
  loudly in tw_session_view.

The other __x86_64__ branches of win32u's Unix files describe the host
CPU (message.c L53, L62 and win32u_private.h L229: memory ordering;
dibdrv/primitives.c L249, L261: inline assembly) and keep their generic
paths.

Line numbers are wine-11.0's dlls/win32u/.

